        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "Granada and Masaya Volcano"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:highlight_text:bd76de8fd4b6e8cf",
      "field": "highlight.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "286ff9b3e0666209b05cfdac432693527532389822ee74b664b1e3e5321c134b",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9om5vj-qfbonkk",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "In Nicaragua, you will explore Granada, one of the country’s oldest colonial cities. The visit includes the main square, the cultural centre at Casa de los Leones, the tower of La Merced Church and the San Francisco Convent.\n\nNext, you will head out onto Lake Nicaragua and visit islands believed to have formed during an eruption of Mombacho Volcano. You will also stop at the private island of Zopango.\n\nYou will then head to Masaya Volcano National Park, home to the Masaya and Nindirí volcanoes, before visiting the Masaya craft market."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_alt:b9ba4fb01410ca70",
      "field": "media.alt",
      "sourceTextSha256": "b8492bc3be8fc134c055631f448575c547ba6869258540a60a27a8036c19feac",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9om5vj-qfbonkk",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "Granada’s yellow cathedral with red domes behind palm trees, Nicaragua"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_hover:92942d95206bb4ec",
      "field": "media.hover",
      "sourceTextSha256": "fbf3344e146a16acc00f765ab5769708349debddcd3ae532d2e2d9236971365f",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9om5vj-qfbonkk",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "Granada: The cathedral towers and domes above the leafy square"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:highlight_title:4640d24aa4d9b200",
      "field": "highlight.title",
      "sourceTextSha256": "53dbe9d4bc500274e2a8615136dae684264ba4d5112a8b10471766fe7ad500ba",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9om5vj-qfbonkk",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "Apoyo Lagoon"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:highlight_text:d53e333407ef0a3e",
      "field": "highlight.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "c2aed1f5346827f23de971ab3dbda68ed0aaf60564df9ecea5226129ed30f204",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9om5vj-qfbonkk",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "The freshwater Apoyo Lagoon formed in the crater of an extinct volcano and is surrounded by dense green vegetation. You can swim, kayak, surf or simply relax by the water.\n\nAfter the sightseeing part of the tour, you will have three days at leisure at the lagoon."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_alt:3bd983aaafb832e1",
      "field": "media.alt",
      "sourceTextSha256": "6ca05dcccf82eeb4122951ccf6f36adf64ad294050147d5052597f23c756b369",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9om5vj-qfbonkk",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "Clear water and a kayaker on Apoyo Lagoon, with the wooded crater slopes behind"
    },
    {
